          "text": "First, I need to identify the positive integers less than 100 that are divisible by 6.\n\nA number is divisible by 6 if it is divisible by both 2 and 3.\n\nTo find the largest such number less than 100, I'll divide 99 by 6, which gives approximately 16.5. Taking the integer part, the largest multiple of 6 under 100 is 96.\n\nNext, I'll list the multiples of 6 from 6 up to 96:\n6, 12, 18, ..., 96.\n\nThis forms an arithmetic sequence where the first term \\( a_1 = 6 \\) and the common difference \\( d = 6 \\).\n\nTo find the number of terms, I'll use the formula for the \\( n \\)-th term of an arithmetic sequence:\n\\[ a_n = a_1 + (n - 1)d \\]\nSetting \\( a_n = 96 \\):\n\\[ 96 = 6 + (n - 1) \\times 6 \\]\n\\[ 90 = (n - 1) \\times 6 \\]\n\\[ n - 1 = 15 \\]\n\\[ n = 16 \\]\n\nTherefore, there are 16 positive integers less than 100 that are divisible by 6.",
